            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ortho.2010.03.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The tissue-based phenomena and the tissue interactions responsible for tooth displacement can be modulated by varying the intensity of the applied forces or by means of medicated molecules absorbed by the patient or prescribed by the orthodontist. However, harmful side-effects such as inflammatory root resorption or replacement resorption (ankylosis) can occur requiring appropriate management on the part of the practitioner.</AbstractText>
